    "knowledge_point": "Computing a Double Summation",
    "problem": "${\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}(i-j)=$",
    "worked_solution": "First, we write out the inner summation by summing over the index $j:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}(i-j) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}[{\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}(i-j)] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}((i-1)+(i-2)+(i-3)) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}(3i-6)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we sum over the index $i:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}(3i-6) & =(3\\cdot 1-6)+(3\\cdot 2-6)+(3\\cdot 3-6) \\\\  & =-3+0+3 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
